    "created_at": "2026-05-29T00:39:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-05-29T00:41:28Z",
    "body": "@slouken recently, there's been a breakthrough with the sensor passthrough stuff, although it's not done thru SDL..\n\nsomeone ( https://github.com/NaokoAF/HastyControls/commit/33556b6c107e69c8fae5c8a6fdcccbe5c31f56d7 , https://github.com/NaokoAF/HastyControls/commit/02fd0e4c22bc01983b22325c182de0ef5474ac4b ) found a way to get ISteamInput's GetMotionSensor working while using SDL Gamepad (but motion goes thru ISteamInput, while SDL goes thru button inputs), **although that method works best if a game already uses Steamworks SDK directly**. Otherwise: a modder will have to provide `steam_api64.dll`/Spacewar themselves. \n\nSo I wonder if possible to do it thru Steam Overlay hooks (something like `SDL_GetGamepadSteamHandle`...?) instead of the DSU method?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
